WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.340
Alaskan Bush People is about a large family
struggling to live off the land in—you guessed

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.340
it—Alaska.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:12.810
But the Brown family may not be struggling
as much as you might think.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:16.290
Here's the real truth about the show...and
the family behind it.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:17.970
BORN RICH

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.220
Billy Bryan Brown admits in his own writing
that he wasn't born in Alaska.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:25.359
He claims to have been born into "a world
of privilege" to a Texas limo company president.

00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:28.650
In his words: "I was given new boats and cars
for my birthdays.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:33.501
I was truly the luckiest kid in town—I had
it all—money, clothes, big ticket toys and

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:35.130
a loving family, too."

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:39.829
Sadly, Brown's parents perished in a plane
crash in 1969, after which Brown says he did

00:00:39.829 --> 00:00:43.129
odd jobs around Texas and New Mexico to make
ends meet.

00:00:43.129 --> 00:00:44.329
TEEN BRIDE

00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:48.530
Radar Online reports that Ami Brown was only
15 years old when she married Billy Bryan

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:49.920
Brown in 1979.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.019
Billy was 26, accounting for an 11 year age
gap.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:55.100
That's illegal in most states today.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.160
And creepy everywhere, always.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.070
PROBABLY RICHER THAN THEY LOOK

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:03.559
While the family's exact net worth is difficult
to determine without examining their tax returns,

00:01:03.559 --> 00:01:06.200
it's safe to assume they're not as poor as
they want us to believe.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.200
Why?

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.570
Well, for one thing, they get paid to be on
television, a deal that's usually at least

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:15.120
kind of lucrative for the participants—no
matter what bushes they like to live in.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.750
BILLY BRYAN BROWN: ACCOMPLISHED WRITER

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:22.290
The family patriarch has over 70 books under
his belt, one of which, One Wave At A Time,

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.590
actually inspired the television show.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:28.250
That's impressive for someone who, ostensibly,
has never used anything beyond candlelight

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:32.500
and fountain pen to write, let alone a typewriter,
computer, or the Internet.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.030
Speaking of…

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:36.240
THE KIDS USE TECHNOLOGY

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:41.490
In 2008, Gabriel Brown (wearing a tank top)
posted a YouTube video about his life.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:44.900
He talks about his father's book tour and
a potential movie deal stemming from One Wave

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:45.900
At A Time.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:50.000
He says it's the first time any of the kids
have been out of the wilderness, "the first

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.520
time we've ever seen a traffic jam," or eaten
fast food.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.510
He says that they'll post videos for the duration
of the tour, which is an odd activity if they're

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.440
not skilled in technology.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:03.440
He ends the video with impersonations of celebrities…the
same celebrities that he'd never have known

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:06.300
about if he didn't have access to television
or the Internet.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.300
Huh?

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:08.580
THE BROWNS MAY HAVE TO LEAVE THE BUSH

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:14.170
Ami Brown suffers from cervical radiculitis,
a form of arthritis in her neck.

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:18.300
She told Radar Online, "It's just something
I think I'm going to have to live with…It

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.030
limits me on things that I can do that I like
to do and enjoy to do.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.070
It definitely makes it harder to live there.

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.350
It's sad and true."

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:27.970
Meanwhile, Billy Bryan Brown's struggles with
seizures have been documented on the show:

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:32.080
if they continue, he'll have to stop pretending
to live like a barbarian for a while and spend

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.660
more time closer to hospitals.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.420
THEY KNOW HOW TO PARTY

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:41.250
Matt Brown was arrested in 2013 for DUI after
what Radar Online describes as a night of

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.010
some pretty hard partying.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.810
He was pulled over for driving drunk and hitting
a parked car in a Walmart parking lot at 4:45

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:51.130
in the morning, after which he "very animatedly"
told his arresting officer about hooking up

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:53.470
with a girl named Julie in a nearby bar.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:57.090
He was sentenced to three days in jail and
18 months of probation.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:00.069
No word on whether or not Julie ever called
him back, though.

00:03:00.069 --> 00:03:02.000
THEY MIGHT BE FRAUDSTERS

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.440
Billy Bryan Brown was charged with 24 counts
of unsworn falsification and theft in January

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.990
2016, while Radar Online reports that Ami
and sons Solomon and Gabe each were charged

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:14.190
with eight counts.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:17.390
Sons Noah and Josh also faced six counts each.

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:21.319
ABC News reports that Brown allegedly lied
on official government applications regarding

00:03:21.319 --> 00:03:26.340
their Alaskan residency in order to receive
Permanent Fund dividend checks from the state.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:30.510
Billy and son Josh pleaded guilty and were
each sentenced to 30 days in jail.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:35.260
The family was ordered to pay $21,000 in restitution
to the state of Alaska.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:39.700
In an official statement on the case, Billy
Brown said, "Alaska's dividend program has

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:43.200
specific requirements for the length of time
in the state, and the reasons for being out

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.500
of Alaska.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.220
Because of the way we live our lives and the
way we often unconventionally travel, I didn't

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:49.830
keep good track of our movements.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:53.830
I accept full responsibility for filing for
benefits without confirming that we met the

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:57.520
requirements…We are committed to living
in Alaska for the long term and we respect

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:58.520
the state's rules.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:02.120
I thought it best to settle to put this behind
us."

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:03.120
Thanks for watching!

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:05.730
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to see more
videos like the one you just saw.

